  id: External_layer_of_sheat_of_recti_abdominis
  partName: External_layer_of_sheat_of_recti_abdominis
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'This structure is a layer of connective tissue that surrounds the rectus abdominis
    muscle and plays a significant role in maintaining abdominal integrity. It supports
    internal organs and helps distribute mechanical forces across the abdominal wall.
    The layer also contributes to posture and core stability by reinforcing the abdominal
    region. '
  - Working with surrounding muscles, it assists in breathing, movement, and protection
    of internal structures, ensuring proper function and structural support of the
    abdominal cavity.
